cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you cite this work, please use the metadata below."
title: "Drape: a negative result on Turtle Graphics as a visual-reasoning probe for language models"
abstract: >-
  We test whether forcing a language model to reproduce an image through imperative
  relative commands, rather than declarative markup, exposes spatial state tracking.
  It does not. The test items are degenerate (a 199-command spiral is reproduced to
  0.27% of its diameter by eight numbers); degeneracy has two independent doors, of
  which only one is normally guarded; degeneracy is a joint property of the shape,
  the grading tolerance, and the search class rather than a property of the shape;
  and the route cannot answer the question it was built for, because every quantity
  the task requires is either readable locally from the image or recomputable by
  summing the model's own emitted tokens.
